<title>JAPAN: Japan June domestic vehicle sales down 5.0 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Japan June domestic vehicle sales down 5.0 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's domestic vehicle sales fell 5.0 percent from a year earlier to 419,059 units in June, the Japan Automobile Dealers' Association (JADA) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>This was the third successive month in which domestic sales fell on a year-on-year basis.</p>
<p>The June sales breakdown was as follows (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Total cars		284,581  down  6.3 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2001 cc    65,986  down  7.4 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc  218,595  down  6.0 percent</p>
<p> Total trucks	    133,384  down  2.1 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy trucks	   11,460  down 14.8 percent</p>
<p> - Light trucks	  121,924  down  0.7 percent</p>
<p> Buses			 1,094  down 19.7 percent</p>
<p>June sales included 32,178 imported vehicles, down 20.5 percent from the year before.</p>
<p>June vehicle sales by five major Japanese makers were as follows (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Toyota Motor     163,249  down  5.8 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Motor	81,013  down 10.9 percent</p>
<p> Honda Motor	 47,420  down  0.3 percent</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors 32,796  down  5.1 percent</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	 25,431  up   27.9 percent</p>
